  "Top conjunctions": `
ug | oog | and | ikaw ug ako. Not og, which marks "a / some".
o | oh | or | tubig o kape = water or coffee.
kon | kohn | if; when (not yet) | Also written kung, as in the card kung gusto nimo.
busa | boo-sah | so; therefore | Careful style; in speech also mao nga.
mao nga | mah-OH ngah | that's why; so | Gikapoy ko, mao nga natulog ko.
aron | ah-rohn | so that; in order to | Nagtuon ko aron makasabot.
samtang | sahm-tahng | while | samtang nagkaon = while eating.
human | hoo-mahn | after; finished | human sa trabaho = after work. Human na = it's done.
sukad | soo-kahd | since | sukad gahapon = since yesterday.
bisan | bee-sahn | even; even though | Bisan gamay = even a little.
maskin | mahs-keen | even if; even | Spanish loan: mas que. Maskin unsa = anything at all.
basta | bahs-tah | as long as; just | Spanish loan: Basta ikaw = as long as it's you.
apan | ah-pahn | but (written) | In speech, pero is far more common.
o kaha | oh kah-hah | or else; or maybe | Kape o kaha tubig?
sa wala pa | sah wah-LAHQ pah | before | sa wala pa ko mokaon = before I eat.
gawas kon | gah-WAHS kohn | unless | Gawas kon moulan = unless it rains.
so | soh | so (English loan) | Very common in Cebu City speech mixed with English.
`,
  "Top interjections": `
Ay! | ai | Oh! | Surprise, small mistakes, or a warm "aw": Ay, salamat!
Aray! | ah-rai | Ouch! | Sudden pain.
Agoy! | ah-goy | Ow! / Oh my! | Pain or dismay; very Cebuano.
Uy! | ooy | Hey! (friendly) | Gets a friend's attention, or "Oh, look!"
Hoy! | hoy | Hey! (sharp) | Can sound rude to a stranger; use Nong or Nang.
Ay sus! | ai soos | Oh, come on! / Oh my! | Mild disbelief or fond impatience.
Wow! | wow | Wow! | English loan, used just as in English.
Grabe! | grah-beh | Too much! / Incredible! | Spanish grave: anything extreme, good or bad.
Kuyaw! | koo-yow | Awesome! / Scary! | Very Cebuano: impressive or dangerous.
Hala ka! | hah-lah kah | You're in trouble now! | Teasing; Hala alone is "Oh no!"
Ha? | hah | Huh? / What? | Didn't hear or can't believe it. At a sentence end, ha = OK?
Hay salamat! | hai sah-LAH-maht | Phew, thank goodness! | Relief.
Sori! | soh-ree | Sorry! | English loan; also written sorry. Careful: Pasayloa ko.
Okay! | oh-kai | OK! | English loan; okay ra = it's fine.
Yehey! | yeh-hay | Yay! | Kids and happy news.
Dali! | dah-LEEQ | Hurry! / Come on! | Also "easy, quick": dali ra.
Bantay! | bahn-tai | Watch out! | Also "guard"; Bantay is a common dog name.
Ayo-ayo! | ah-yoh ah-yoh | Be careful! / Take care! | Said when someone leaves or does something risky.
Ania! | ah-nee-ah | Here it is! | Handing something over or finding it.
Kalami! | kah-lah-mee | So delicious! | ka- + lami: how tasty!
Pastilan! | pahs-tee-lahn | Good grief! | Older people's exclamation; heard in the province.
Tan-awa! | tahn-ah-wah | Look! | The command form of tan-aw.
Mao ba? | mah-OH bah | Is that so? | Interested reaction to news.
`,
